#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:1
msgid "Building Asterinas on Asterinas"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:3
msgid ""
"Asterinas is capable of _self-hosting_: the tools that produce the kernel "
"can run on the kernel itself. This page demonstrates how one can use "
"Asterinas NixOS to build Asterinas from source and boot the freshly built "
"kernel in a nested VM. Along the way, Nix, Cargo, rustc, and QEMU all run on "
"Asterinas, which makes a self-hosted build one of the largest real-world "
"workloads the kernel has been put through."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:12
msgid ""
"This capability is still experimental. The procedure on this page has been "
"verified only on x86-64, and only up to the point where the nested kernel "
"reports a successful boot."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:16
msgid "Before you begin"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:18
msgid ""
"You need an x86-64 Linux host with KVM. On the host, set up either the "
"Docker container from [Getting Started](../kernel/#getting-started) or the "
"[Nix development shell](../kernel/nix-development.md), and run the host "
"commands on this page inside it. The host needs about 50 GiB of free disk "
"space, enough memory to give the VM 40 GiB, and Internet access, because the "
"VM downloads the source, Nix packages, and Rust crates."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:28
msgid ""
"Depending on the host's performance, expect the installation to take about "
"30 minutes and the first build inside the VM to take more than an hour."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:32
msgid "Install Asterinas NixOS"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:34
msgid ""
"Install Asterinas NixOS as described for [kernel developers](../distro/"
"#kernel-developers), but with a 32 GiB disk. The default 16 GiB disk leaves "
"too little room. The development shell alone takes about 6 GiB, and after "
"the first build the VM uses about 18 GiB."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:41
msgid "In the Docker container, run:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:47
msgid ""
"The [Nix development shell](../kernel/nix-development.md#enter-the-"
"development-shell) runs without root privileges, and `make nixos` needs them "
"to set up a loop device, so in the shell, install from the ISO image instead:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:57
msgid ""
"`make run_iso` installs Asterinas NixOS in a VM without further input and "
"exits when the installation finishes."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:60
msgid "Start the VM"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:62
msgid "Boot the installed disk with 40 GiB of memory and four vCPUs:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:68
msgid ""
"Do not give the VM less memory. Asterinas does not yet free cached file data "
"under memory pressure, so everything the VM downloads or builds stays in "
"memory, and the VM uses about 31 GiB by the end of `make kernel`. With 32 "
"GiB and eight vCPUs, the kernel sometimes ran out of memory near the end of "
"the build."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:75
msgid ""
"The console logs in as root automatically. To stop the VM, run `sync` and "
"then `poweroff`. Typing `exit` does not stop it, because the console logs in "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:79
msgid "Get the source"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:81
msgid ""
"The image does not include the Asterinas source. Clone it inside the VM:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:88
msgid ""
"The VM does not share files with the host. To build your own changes, push "
"them to a branch the VM can reach, such as one in your fork, and clone that "
"branch with `--branch`."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:92
msgid ""
"Use `git clone` rather than downloading a source archive. Nix copies only "
"tracked files from a Git checkout into its store. From a plain directory, it "
"copies everything, including ignored build output such as `target/`."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:97
msgid "Build the kernel inside the VM"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:99
msgid "Enter the development shell from the checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:106
msgid ""
"The flake declares the project's binary caches on Cachix. Without `--accept-"
"flake-config`, Nix first asks whether to accept them. The image already uses "
"the same caches, so the answer changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:110
msgid ""
"The first run downloads about 6 GiB of packages and builds the ones that no "
"binary cache provides. Then build the kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:118
msgid "Boot the kernel you built"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:120
msgid ""
"In the development shell inside the VM, boot the new kernel in a nested VM:"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:132
msgid ""
"Asterinas does not provide KVM, so `ENABLE_KVM=0` runs the nested VM under "
"QEMU's software emulation, and booting takes a few minutes. `NETDEV=none` "
"and `QEMU_DISPLAY=none` turn off networking and VNC, because QEMU cannot "
"open their listening sockets inside Asterinas. `MEM=2G` keeps the nested VM "
"small."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:139
msgid ""
"With `AUTO_TEST=boot`, the new kernel prints `Successfully booted.` once it "
"boots, and the nested VM then exits on its own. `make run_kernel` itself "
"does not return on Asterinas yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:143
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:145
msgid ""
"Only the boot test has been run in the nested VM. The nested VM has no "
"network or display, so tests that need them cannot run there."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:148
msgid ""
"The nested VM runs under software emulation, so even the boot test takes a "
"few minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/distro/building-on-asterinas.md:150
msgid ""
"Nix inside the VM builds as root and without a sandbox, because Asterinas "
"does not yet support the isolation that Nix relies on. Builds are therefore "
"not isolated from the rest of the system."
msgstr ""
